// The caret is one number over the whole document; a run is where the text
// actually lives. This is the translation between them.
//
// Runs are walked rather than indexed because a document holds tens of them
// and the alternative is a running total kept correct through every edit --
// a second representation of the same fact, and the one that goes wrong.

ed_rcp(int r) {
  string s = odt_run_text(r);
  int ret_i = ed_cps(s);
} return int ret_i;
given odt_doc_fixture (0):(2)
given ed_step_fixture2 (0):(2)

// Which run holds code point k. The last run is the answer for anything at or
// past the end of the document, so that typing with the caret at the very end
// appends to the last run rather than indexing past it.
ed_run_of(int k) {
  int r = 0;
  while(r < odt_runs() - 1 && k >= ed_rcp(r)) {
    k = k - ed_rcp(r);
    r = r + 1;
  }
} return int r;
given ed_step_fixture (0):(0) then calls ed_rcp:[0]
given ed_step_fixture (999999):(0) then calls ed_rcp:[0]

// How many code points precede run r.
ed_pre(int r) {
  int n = 0;
  int i = 0;
  while(i < r) {
    n = n + ed_rcp(i);
    i = i + 1;
  }
} return int n;
